-- title:
--   Toric and old lattices in TₚJ₁(M) for p ∥ M
-- statement:
--   Let $M$ be a non-zero natural number and $p$ a prime with $p \mid M$ and $p^2 \nmid M$, and let $P$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` lying over $p$, in the sense that $p$ belongs to the non-units of $P$. Write $T =$ [`TateModule p (JOne M)`](def/EllipticCurve_TateModule.html#L15), the $\mathbb Z_p$-module of sequences $(x_n)$ in $J_1(M) = \mathrm{Pic}^0$ of the base-changed function field `x1FunctionFieldBar M` with $p^n x_n = 0$ and $p\,x_{n+1} = x_n$, equipped with the action [`TateModule.rep`](def/EllipticCurve_TateModule.html#L174) of $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)$ on coefficients and with the action `tateHeckeRepOne` of the polynomial Hecke algebra `HeckeAlgOne` $= \mathbb Z[X_i : i \in \mathrm{Primes} \sqcup \mathbb N]$ through the module structure `heckeModuleOneBar`, whose generators are written $T_\ell =$ `heckeGenOne ℓ` and $\langle d\rangle =$ `diamondGen d`; the same structure is used for level $M/p$. The assertion is the existence of $\mathbb Z_p$-submodules $T^{\mathrm t}, T^{\mathrm{old}} \subseteq T$ and $\mathbb Z_p$-linear maps $\pi_0, \pi_1 \colon T_p J_1(M/p) \to T$ such that: $T^{\mathrm t}$ is stable under every element of `HeckeAlgOne` and under every element of the decomposition subgroup of $P$ over $\mathbb Q$; there is $k \in \mathbb N$ with $p^k(\tau x - x) \in T^{\mathrm{old}} + T^{\mathrm t}$ for all $\tau$ in the image in $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)$ of the inertia subgroup of $P$ and all $x$ in the range of the diamond norm $\sum_d \langle d\rangle$, the sum over $d < M$ coprime to $M$ with $d \equiv 1 \pmod{M/p}$; each such $\tau$ acts on $T^{\mathrm t}$ by the scalar $\chi_p(\tau) \in \mathbb Z_p^\times$ given by the cyclotomic character; for every $\varphi$ which is a Frobenius at $P$ for $p$ (that is, $\varphi$ lies in the decomposition subgroup and acts as $x \mapsto x^p$ on the residue field of $P$) and every $x \in T^{\mathrm t}$, both $T_p(\varphi x)$ and $\varphi(T_p x)$ equal $\chi_p(\varphi)\,x$; each of $\pi_0, \pi_1$ commutes with $T_\ell$ and with $\langle \ell \rangle$ for every prime $\ell \nmid M$; $T^{\mathrm{old}}$ is the sum of the ranges of $\pi_0$ and $\pi_1$; and $T^{\mathrm{old}} \cap T^{\mathrm t} = 0$.
--
--   This packages the local behaviour at a prime $p$ exactly dividing the level of the $p$-adic Tate module of the Jacobian of $X_1(M)$: the toric part coming from the multiplicative reduction of the Deligne–Rapoport model, on which inertia acts by the cyclotomic character and $U_p$ acts as Frobenius times $\chi_p$, the old part generated by the two degeneracy maps from level $M/p$, and the statement that inertia acts trivially on the diamond-norm part modulo the sum of the two. It supplies the local input for [`ModularCurve.exists_ordLine_frobenius_sub_smul_mem_tateModule_jOne_quotient_of_diamond_eq_one_of_forall_linearMap_eq_zero_of_dvd_of_not_sq_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.exists_ordLine_frobenius_sub_smul_mem_tateModule_jOne_quotient_of_diamond_eq_one_of_forall_linearMap_eq_zero_of_dvd_of_not_sq_dvd), in the multiplicative ($p$-new) case of the level-lowering argument.
